      "body": "### Project URL\n\nhttps://github.com/blkdmr/smle\n\n### Category\n\nPython\n\n### Project Title\n\nSMLE is a lightweight Python framework designed to automate the \"boring stuff\" in ML projects so developers can focus on the model.\n\n### Project Description\n\nSMLE automates ML boilerplate like config parsing, logging, and WandB tracking. It helps developers focus on models and teaches beginners clean project structure without the setup headache\n\n### Highlights\n\nUnlike complex configuration libraries (like Hydra) that require steep learning curves, SMLE stands out for its minimalism and speed. It combines configuration management, logging, and experiment tracking into a single lightweight wrapper.\n\n### Example Code\n\n```markdown\nfrom smle import SMLE\n\napp = SMLE()\n\n# Your yaml-based config is automatically injected into 'args'\n@app.entrypoint\ndef main(args):\n    print(f\"Training with lr: {args['training']['lr']}\") \n    # This print is automatically logged locally and synced to WandB if enabled\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    app.run()\n```\n\n### Screenshots or Demo Videos\n\n_No response_",
